          "id": "bell_pavilion",
          "mode": "landmark",
          "brief": "A feudal Japanese temple belfry (shoro) pavilion standing on an elevated dressed stone plinth. Four heavy dark timber pillars support an upturned hip-and-gable tiled roof with wooden bracket complexes. Suspended within is a massive cast bronze temple bell (bonsho) hung by heavy iron chains, flanked by a horizontal wooden striking log hung from hemp cords.",
          "envelope": [
            13,
            16,
            13
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
